{"type":"compaction","id":"b90cbdc3","parentId":"80aaaae2","timestamp":"2026-06-02T04:45:44.480Z","summary":"## Goal\n- Develop a Python script for data processing.\n- Integrate machine learning model into the existing application.\n\n## Constraints & Preferences\n- Use pandas and scikit-learn libraries.\n- Ensure code is readable and well-commented.\n\n## Progress\n### Done\n- [x] Installed necessary libraries: `pandas`, `scikit-learn`.\n- [x] Loaded dataset using pandas.\n- [x] Cleaned the data by handling missing values.\n- [x] Preprocessed the data for machine learning model integration.\n- [x] Defined feature and target variables.\n- [x] Split data into training and testing sets.\n\n### In Progress\n- [ ] Implement machine learning model.\n- [ ] Evaluate the model performance.\n\n### Blocked\n- [ ]\n\n## Key Decisions\n- **Use `SimpleImputer` from scikit-learn for missing value handling**: Simplifies code and ensures consistency.\n- **Preprocessing steps before implementing the model**: Ensures that the data is in a suitable format for training the machine learning model.\n\n## Next Steps\n1. Implement machine learning model using existing preprocessing steps.\n2. Evaluate the model performance on the test set.\n\n## Critical Context\n- Dataset is located at `/data/sample_data.csv`.\n- Existing application structure can be found in `app/main.py`.","firstKeptEntryId":"794d6b0a","tokensBefore":13508,"details":{"readFiles":[],"modifiedFiles":[]},"fromHook":false}
